<title>UK: UK's Brown says budget is for long-term stability.</title>
<headline>UK's Brown says budget is for long-term stability.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown said on Wednesday his budget would be aimed at long-term fiscal stability.</p>
<p>In his first budget speech to parliament, Brown said his decision to give the Bank of England freedom to set interest rates signified his determination to break from short-termism.</p>
<p>&quot;In this budget I will match these measures for long-term monetary stability with measures designed to promote long-term fiscal stability,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
